# D-93. The host calls its own capturing model before the return: the call builds the node the
# return would build, with the host's values at the call, and calls it (a capture is read-only in
# the model, so that node is exactly what the host sees there).  makeAdder 5: q = addN(1) with
# n 5 = 6; n becomes 15; r = addN(1) with n 15 = 16; n becomes q + r = 22; the returned node
# captures n 22: add(1) = 23.  The base translator refused ("a callable merge host names a nested
# method outside the return").  Mutants: the call through the model's own native function (its
# stub returns 0) -- 1, not 23, exit 1; the call's node without its capture -- "walk error:
# INVALID", exit 3.  Entry 7.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    int: q (addN: 1)
    n: n + 10
    int: r (addN: 1)
    n: q + r
    return: addN

add: makeAdder 5
int: a (add: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 23
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
